{"step_index":1116,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-21T19:14:48Z","thinking":"**Analyzing Startup Configuration**\n\nI've just realized a critical detail in `App.xaml`. There's no `StartupUri` defined! This changes everything. WPF's default behavior is to handle the application startup if there's no `StartupUri`, leading to the `Main` method with `InitializeComponent` and `Run`. This clarifies the initial application flow.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"replace_file_content","args":{"AllowMultiple":"false","Description":"\"Add StartupUri to App.xaml.\"","EndLine":"7","Instruction":"\"Add StartupUri attribute to Application tag\"","ReplacementContent":"\"<Application x:Class=\\\"Spectra.App\\\"\\n             xmlns=\\\"http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation\\\"\\n             xmlns:x=\\\"http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml\\\"\\n             StartupUri=\\\"UI/MainWindow.xaml\\\">\\n    <Application.Resources>\\n         \\n    </Application.Resources>\\n</Application>\"","StartLine":"1","TargetContent":"\"<Application x:Class=\\\"Spectra.App\\\"\\n             xmlns=\\\"http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation\\\"\\n             xmlns:x=\\\"http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml\\\">\\n    <Application.Resources>\\n         \\n    </Application.Resources>\\n</Application>\"","TargetFile":"\"c:\\\\Users\\\\Arthur Henrique\\\\Documents\\\\GitHub\\\\Spectra\\\\src-csharp\\\\App.xaml\"","toolAction":"\"Adding StartupUri to App.xaml\"","toolSummary":"\"Update App.xaml StartupUri\""}}]}
